 "gates_doc": "scripts/levels/c4/annex_level.gd (extends the registry level): an entry with \"scene\" is built only when the level plays that Story scene (level_id, set before _ready); actors carry \"scene_id\". \"after\" / \"until\" / \"choice\" / \"fade\" are the registry gates (objectives of earlier scenes count as complete). Lights carry an empty \"after\" so they are named and their slow flicker runs. camera_zones = the camera window per scene; looks = canvas modulate + grade per scene.",
 "notes": [
  "Side view: feet line y 300, walk band 296-306, x 18-1902; everything painted stands behind it (base_y <= 294), the fg layers stay below y 318. The tarpaulin (858-898) is the permanent blocker between scene A (back yard and coal stage, Monday dawn) and scene B (showcase and platform 1, Tuesday evening): two places, two bakes (depot_a / depot_b), never seen together (camera_zones).",
  "People: Kolonne 4 (ten life strips + Maria, the speaking NPC at x 578), the cook (seen through the hatch), a stoker and a fitter in A; in B the brass band (five different people on one beat; the tuba is the turntable man, bareheaded -- his cap lies on the controller), children, the cleaner, the canteen's waitress and cook, an old fitter oiling the turntable, a smoker in the sand-house door, a woman sifting sand, the depot cat, the militia patrol (grey greatcoats, fur hats), the families of the explore text, the grandmother, the conductor (navy, silver cap band, lantern), a mother and boy, a couple, the pirozhki seller, the porter (quilted jacket, white apron) -- anonymous, no insignia. Irina, Maria, the guard, Ekdahl, the press officer and Lev stand at the npcs anchors (cast stream sheets).",
  "Readable story figures (scene.json \"readable\": no life strip, sparrow or NPC covers them): the carbon on Irina's sill (order_taken removes it), the duty blackboard, the press notice on the roundhouse back door, „РАЗДАЧА“ over the hatch, „ВОССТАНОВИМ ВМЕСТЕ“ on the old banner (5x7) and on the tarpaulin panel (lashed in front of its poles), the brass plate „1939“, the guidebook on the press table (book_taken), the halves / the joined card on Lev's bench, „БЕРЛИН – КАРСК“ / „СПАЛЬНЫЙ ВАГОН“ / „ВАГОН-РЕСТОРАН“ on the express's letterboard above the windows (over the people's heads), the two clocks and „ВЫХОД НА ПЕРРОН“ on the gate's iron bracket.",
  "Insignia: patches/insignia_*.png (roundhouse gable, roundhouse front, the engine's smokebox door) show the fictional gear-and-wheat emblem; their *_hist twins the red star with hammer and sickle (Symbols.pick). No life strip carries insignia.",
  "Palette: data/chapters/c4p2.json palettes.depot + the ramps of env_c4p2_karsk_kit.DEPOT (integration note of the env-karsk stream)."
 ],
